  <section class="msv__section">
    <div class="msv__container">
      <div class="msv__section-hd">
        <h2>India-Specific Document Requirements</h2>
        <p>Indian students must provide several documents specific to India's regulatory framework. These are in addition to standard student visa requirements (acceptance letter, proof of funds, health insurance, etc.).</p>
      </div>

      <div class="msv__steps">
        <div class="msv__step">
          <div class="msv__step-num">1</div>
          <div class="msv__step-body">
            <h3>Police Clearance Certificate (PCC)</h3>
            <p>Obtained from the Passport Seva Kendra. Apply online at passportindia.gov.in or visit your nearest centre in person. Processing takes 7-15 days. The PCC is valid for 6 months and must be apostilled by the Ministry of External Affairs. Cost: approx. INR 500-800.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="msv__step">
          <div class="msv__step-num">2</div>
          <div class="msv__step-body">
            <h3>MEA Apostille for All Documents</h3>
            <p>All Indian documents (PCC, educational certificates, birth certificate, affidavits) must be apostilled by the Ministry of External Affairs (MEA). Apply online at mea.gov.in/apostille or visit MEA offices in major cities. Processing: 5-10 working days. Cost: approx. INR 100-200 per document.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="msv__step">
          <div class="msv__step-num">3</div>
          <div class="msv__step-body">
            <h3>Sworn Spanish Translation</h3>
            <p>All documents must be translated into Spanish by a certified/sworn translator. English documents (including your PCC) still require sworn translation into Spanish — English versions alone are not sufficient. Find sworn translators in your city or use authorised online services. Cost: INR 1,500-3,000 per document.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="msv__step">
          <div class="msv__step-num">4</div>
          <div class="msv__step-body">
            <h3>Indian Bank Statements</h3>
            <p>Demonstrate financial capacity with 3-6 months of bank statements. The Spanish consulate assesses your funds in EUR equivalent. Fixed deposits (FDs), savings accounts, and recurring deposits (RDs) are all acceptable. Must be in your name or (for parental sponsorship) in your parents' names with an affidavit of support.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="msv__step">
          <div class="msv__step-num">5</div>
          <div class="msv__step-body">
            <h3>Parental Sponsorship (if applicable)</h3>
            <p>Very common for Indian students. Required documents: (1) Notarised affidavit of support from parents; (2) Parents' bank statements (3-6 months); (3) Latest Income Tax Returns (ITR) from both parents; (4) Parents' identity proof (copy of passport or PAN card). The affidavit must be notarised by a notary public and apostilled by MEA.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="msv__step">
          <div class="msv__step-num">6</div>
          <div class="msv__step-body">
            <h3>Indian Passport</h3>
            <p>Must be valid for at least 1 year from your course start date. You need 2 blank pages in your passport for the Spanish visa sticker. If your passport expires soon, renew it before applying.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="msv__step">
          <div class="msv__step-num">7</div>
          <div class="msv__step-body">
            <h3>Academic Transcripts & Certificates</h3>
            <p>For university admissions. School/college certificates may need to be apostilled and/or attested. Check your university's specific requirements — some Spanish universities require official transcripts directly from your institution.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

