  <!-- ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ FINANCIAL REQUIREMENTS ════ -->
  <section class="msv__section">
    <div class="msv__container">
      <div class="msv__section-hd">
        <h2>Financial Requirements for Indian Students</h2>
        <p>The Spanish consulate uses the IPREM threshold to assess your financial capacity. Here's what you need to know when demonstrating funds in Indian Rupees.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="msv__alert msv__alert--warn">
        <span class="msv__alert-icon">⚠️</span>
        <p><strong>IPREM Threshold 2026:</strong> Approximately EUR 815-850 per month. For a typical 9-month Master's programme, you should demonstrate access to funds equivalent to EUR 7,300-8,000 (approx. INR 6,50,000-7,15,000 at current exchange rates). Check the latest IPREM on the Spanish government website — it updates annually.</p>
      </div>

      <h3 style="margin-top: 2rem; margin-bottom: 1rem;">Acceptable Ways to Show Funds (in INR)</h3>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Savings account:</strong> Regular balance in your name. Provide 3-6 months of statements showing consistent balance above the threshold.</li>
        <li><strong>Fixed deposits (FDs):</strong> Very commonly accepted. Can be in your name or pledged by parents. Most consulates accept FDs as "liquid" proof of funds.</li>
        <li><strong>Education loans:</strong> Loan sanction letter from an Indian bank showing the loan amount (e.g., INR 25 lakhs). Must cover your full course cost.</li>
        <li><strong>Scholarship letters:</strong> If you have a scholarship, include the award letter. You may still need to show additional funds for personal expenses.</li>
        <li><strong>Parental support:</strong> Most common for Indian students. Parents' bank statements + ITRs + notarised affidavit. The affidavit states that parents will fund your studies.</li>
        <li><strong>Recurring deposits (RDs):</strong> Similar to FDs; shows monthly savings and commitment to financial discipline.</li>
      </ul>

      <div class="msv__alert msv__alert--info" style="margin-top: 2rem;">
        <span class="msv__alert-icon">💡</span>
        <p><strong>Exchange rate note:</strong> The consulate will convert INR to EUR using official rates at the time of assessment. Exchange rates fluctuate, so demonstrate slightly more than the minimum threshold to be safe. Showing 20-30% above the requirement is standard practice.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

