  <!-- ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ FAQs ════ -->
  <section class="msv__section msv__section--cream">
    <div class="msv__container">
      <div class="msv__section-hd">
        <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
        <p>Answers to the most common questions from Indian student visa applicants.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="msv__faq-list">
        <details>
          <summary>Do Indian students need a visa for Spain?</summary>
          <div class="msv__faq-answer">
            <p>Yes. Indian nationals require a Spain Student Visa to study in Spain. The visa is issued for the duration of your studies (typically 9 months to 2 years, depending on your course). It's processed through the Spanish Embassy in New Delhi or VFS Global centres.</p>
          </div>
        </details>

        <details>
          <summary>How do I get a police clearance certificate in India?</summary>
          <div class="msv__faq-answer">
            <p>Police clearance certificates (PCC) are obtained from the Passport Seva Kendra. You can apply online at <strong>passportindia.gov.in</strong>, or visit your nearest Passport Seva Kendra in person. Processing typically takes 7-15 days. The PCC is valid for 6 months. After receiving it, you must get it apostilled by the Ministry of External Affairs (MEA) — this is a mandatory step before submission to the Spanish consulate.</p>
          </div>
        </details>

        <details>
          <summary>Where do I apostille my documents in India?</summary>
          <div class="msv__faq-answer">
            <p>All Indian documents (PCC, educational certificates, affidavits) must be apostilled by the Ministry of External Affairs (MEA). You can apply online at <strong>mea.gov.in/apostille</strong> or visit your nearest MEA office in person. Processing typically takes 5-10 working days. Each document requires separate apostille. Cost is approximately INR 100-200 per document.</p>
          </div>
        </details>

        <details>
          <summary>Can my parents sponsor my student visa?</summary>
          <div class="msv__faq-answer">
            <p>Yes. Parental sponsorship is very common for Indian students applying for Spanish student visas. You will need: (1) A notarised affidavit of support from your parents; (2) Your parents' bank statements (3-6 months); (3) Your parents' latest Income Tax Returns (ITR); (4) Your parents' identity proof. The affidavit must be notarised and apostilled by MEA before submission. This demonstrates that your parents have the financial capacity to support your studies abroad.</p>
          </div>
        </details>

        <details>
          <summary>How much money do I need in my bank account?</summary>
          <div class="msv__faq-answer">
            <p>The Spanish consulate assesses financial capacity based on the IPREM threshold, which is approximately EUR 815-850 per month in 2026. For a typical 9-month Master's programme, you should demonstrate access to funds equivalent to EUR 7,300-8,000 (approximately INR 6,50,000-7,15,000 at current rates). This can come from your own savings, fixed deposits, education loans, scholarships, or parental support. It's good practice to show 20-30% above the minimum threshold. Fixed deposits are particularly popular with Indian applicants and are widely accepted by Spanish consulates.</p>
          </div>
        </details>

        <details>
          <summary>Can I work in Spain after my studies?</summary>
          <div class="msv__faq-answer">
            <p>Yes. After you complete your official degree, you can apply for a Job Seeker Visa (valid 12 months), which allows you to search for employment in Spain. Once you secure a job, your employer can sponsor you for a Work Permit (Tarjeta de Residencia y de Trabajo). After 5 years of continuous work residency, you can apply for a Long-Term Residency Visa. <strong>Important:</strong> Spain offers 10-year standard residency-to-citizenship. Indian nationals do not qualify for the 2-year fast-track citizenship (which is only for former Spanish colonies).</p>
          </div>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>How long does the student visa process take for Indian applicants?</summary>
          <div class="msv__faq-answer">
            <p>Processing for Indian applicants is similar to other nationalities: 4-8 weeks after the consulate appointment. The main Spanish consulate serving India is in New Delhi, with a consulate in Mumbai. Appointment availability varies — book as early as possible.</p>
          </div>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>What income evidence do Indian students need?</summary>
          <div class="msv__faq-answer">
            <p>Indian students typically need recent bank statements showing sufficient funds (approximately ₹55,000-65,000+ per month or equivalent in savings), scholarship documentation if applicable, parental support letters if parents are sponsoring, and parents' bank statements. Documents should be in English or accompanied by sworn translations.</p>
          </div>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>Do Indian students need a DELE certificate to study in Spain?</summary>
          <div class="msv__faq-answer">
            <p>For Spanish-taught programmes, most universities require B2 Spanish proficiency (DELE B2 or equivalent). For English-taught programmes, an English proficiency certificate (IELTS or equivalent) is typically required instead. Language schools have no prior Spanish requirement.</p>
          </div>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>Can Indian students work in Spain on a student visa?</summary>
          <div class="msv__faq-answer">
            <p>Yes, up to 30 hours per week with work authorisation, the same as any other non-EU student. Work in India-facing companies or remote work for Indian employers while in Spain is an increasingly common approach for Indian digital workers studying in Spain.</p>
          </div>
        </details>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

